cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Digital Legacy Provider Comparison"
message: "If you use this dataset or quote the teardown, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A structured, primary-source comparison of what every major password manager,
  platform legacy-contact feature and dedicated digital-legacy service actually
  does when a user dies. Each of the sixteen records is scored on two questions:
  does the provider verify that the user actually died, and can the provider read
  the user's data. Every field carries the source URL it was read from, and any
  field that could not be established from a primary source is recorded as
  "unknown" rather than guessed. The dataset's central finding is that verifying
  death and being unable to read the user's data are, across every record,
  mutually exclusive.
